use companion

Test rig: all 22 slots mapped (slot[k] = k), every W0 and PB is identity, positions (x, y, z): 0 hips (0, 1, 0), 1 spine (0, 1.1, 0), 2 chest (0, 1.2, 0), 3 upper_chest (0, 1.3, 0), 4 neck (0, 1.45, 0), 5 head (0, 1.55, 0), 6 l_shoulder (0.05, 1.4, 0), 7 l_upper_arm (0.15, 1.4, 0), 8 l_lower_arm (0.4, 1.4, 0), 9 l_hand (0.65, 1.4, 0), 10 to 13 the same with x negated, 14 l_upper_leg (0.1, 0.95, 0), 15 l_lower_leg (0.1, 0.5, 0), 16 l_foot (0.1, 0.08, 0), 17 l_toes (0.1, 0, 0.12), 18 to 21 the same with x negated. `pack_rest(pos real[:], out real[:])` builds a rest pack (12 reals per slot, layout of `motion`) with identity rotations, the given positions and mapped flag 1. Print quaternions as `name x y z w` with `rig::slot_name` and each component with 4 decimals, printing 0.0000 for any value whose magnitude is below 0.00005.

Every want and out array has 110 reals (5 per slot, the layout of `motion`). Case 1: `motion::solve_local` with no wants; print `rest ok` when every output rotation is within 1e-9 of identity in every component, else `rest bad`. Case 2: a direction want (0, -1, 0) on slot 7 only; print slots 7 and 8 from the output. Case 3: `motion::pose_solve` without mirror on landmarks that are all at (0, 0, 0) with visibility 1 except: 23 (0.1, 0, 0), 24 (-0.1, 0, 0), 11 (0.18, -0.45, 0), 12 (-0.18, -0.45, 0), 13 (0.18, -0.15, 0), 15 (0.18, 0.1, 0), 14 (-0.45, -0.45, 0), 16 (-0.7, -0.45, 0); every other landmark has visibility 0. Print the returned count prefixed `count`, then slots 7 and 11 prefixed `pose`. Case 4: the same landmarks with mirror; print slots 11 and 7 prefixed `mirror`. Case 5: a target rig equal to the test rig except slot 8 at (0.15 + 0.25·0.70710678, 1.4 - 0.25·0.70710678, 0) and slot 9 at (0.15 + 0.5·0.70710678, 1.4 - 0.5·0.70710678, 0); `motion::retarget_clip` with the test rig as source, one frame whose source world rotations are all identity and whose hips position is (0, 1, 0); print target slots 7 and 8 prefixed `retarget`, then the hips position as `hips 0.0000 1.0000 0.0000`-style with 4 decimals. Case 6: a target rig equal to the test rig except slot 15 at (0.2, 0.5, 0) and slot 16 at (0.3, 0.08, 0) (legs splayed outward); `motion::retarget_clip` with the test rig as source and one frame of all-identity source rotations with hips at (0, 1, 0); print target slots 14 and 15 prefixed `legs` (foot IK keeps the foot under the source's foot, so the splayed legs straighten and the knee bends forward). Case 7: a target rig equal to the test rig except slot 16 at (0.1, 0.12, 0), slot 20 at (-0.1, 0.12, 0), slot 17 at (0.1, 0.04, 0.12) and slot 21 at (-0.1, 0.04, 0.12); `motion::retarget_clip` with the test rig as source and one frame whose source world rotations are identity except slot 14, which is `qm::q_axis_angle` about (1, 0, 0) by -0.52359878 radians (the knee swings forward), with hips at (0, 1, 0); print target slots 14 and 15 prefixed `ik`.

